          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: کارآگاه",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "کارآگاه (kârâgâh) — \"a detective\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "کارآگاه (kârâgâh) همه چیز را با دقت نگاه کرد. Kârâgâh hame chiz râ bâ deqqat negâh kard. The detective looked at everything carefully."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "kâr \"work\" + âgâh \"aware\": one who is aware of the case."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "kârâgâh is a modern compound built from Persian kâr \"work\" and âgâh \"aware, informed\", both native words."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
