              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ردپا (radd-e pâ) — \"a footprint, a trace\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "روی برف ردپای یک گرگ بود. Ru-ye barf radd-e pâ-ye yek gorg bud. There were a wolf's footprints in the snow."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "radd \"trace\" + pâ \"foot\". Also figurative: the trace someone left behind."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pâ \"foot\" is inherited Persian. The origin of radd \"trace, track\" is not settled, and EtymDB lists no entry."
            }
          ]
        },
